{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Maven multi-module builds; new projects are created as Maven modules within the respective repositories (s-c-d, s-c-s, SI).",
    "For U1, configure the build (maven-shade-plugin or Gradle shadow) to place external libraries on the classpath ahead of bundled classes (e.g., via manifest Class-Path or a dedicated lib folder and parent-first classloading) so they override uber-jar classes.",
    "For U2 and U4, create dedicated modules with clear package names; the @RedisRule contract is placed in a separate test-jar or spring-integration-commons-test module.",
    "For U3, port the SFTP module as a Spring Cloud Stream Source using Spring Integration SFTP inbound adapter, bound via @ConfigurationProperties.",
    "For U5, introduce a base auto-configuration / ModuleType.PROCESSOR foundation that registers processor modules from s-c-s-m as OOTB modules.",
    "For U6, extend AetherModuleResolver with an offline flag that sets RepositorySystemSession.setOffline(true) and uses only the local Maven repository.",
    "For U7, define a ModuleRegistry interface (getModuleInfo, list, register, unregister) and provide an in-memory implementation keyed by module name/coordinates.",
    "For U8, implement Spring Shell @ShellComponent commands (module info, list, register, unregister) delegating to the ModuleRegistry.",
    "Baseline on Java 17, Spring Framework 6, and Spring Boot 3 as required by the spec."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced Spring developer performs all work with an existing local environment (JDK 17, Maven, Git, IDE).",
    "The abbreviations map as follows: s-c-d = Spring Cloud Data Flow, s-c-s = Spring Cloud Stream, s-c-s-m = Spring Cloud Stream Modules, SI = Spring Integration, XD = Spring XD.",
    "The external library referenced in U1/U2 is of moderate size and currently embedded in the uber-jar; moving it is a refactoring task without major behavioral change.",
    "Spring XD SFTP module source is accessible and can be adapted without legal or licensing obstacles.",
    "For U4, an embedded Redis (or Testcontainers Redis) is available for the @RedisRule test infrastructure.",
    "The s-c-s-m processor modules already exist; U5 only requires the foundation to consume them, not creating the modules themselves.",
    "ModuleRegistry initial implementation uses in-memory storage; no external database or persistent store is required for this increment.",
    "Effort estimates include writing unit tests and minimal documentation (README/help text); no separate performance, security, or production deployment work is included.",
    "Existing CI pipelines will automatically pick up new modules once they are committed; CI configuration changes are out of scope."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-01",
      "activity_name": "Uber-jar external library override",
      "activity_description": "Modify the s-c-d build configuration (maven-shade or Gradle shadow) so that external libraries are placed on the classpath ahead of bundled classes, allowing them to override any existing library in the uber-jar. Includes verification test.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-02",
      "activity_name": "Extract external library to own project",
      "activity_description": "Create a new Maven module/project for the external library within the s-c-d repo, move the code, adjust imports and dependencies to achieve clear separation of functionalities.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-03",
      "activity_name": "Port SFTP module to s-c-s",
      "activity_description": "Port the Spring XD SFTP module into the s-c-s repo as a source module for streaming pipelines, using Spring Integration SFTP adapters, configuration properties, and integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-04",
      "activity_name": "Create @RedisRule test project",
      "activity_description": "Create a new project/module containing the @RedisRule annotation and test execution contract, isolate it from core functionalities, and make it reusable for test coverage (potentially under SI commons).",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-05",
      "activity_name": "Processor OOTB foundation",
      "activity_description": "Create the foundation (base classes / auto-configuration) in s-c-d to support processor modules as OOTB, enabling reuse of processor modules from the s-c-s-m repo in streaming pipelines.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-06",
      "activity_name": "Offline mode for AetherModuleResolver",
      "activity_description": "Enable an offline mode flag in AetherModuleResolver (s-c-s) so module artifacts are resolved from the local Maven repository instead of a remote repository.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-07",
      "activity_name": "ModuleRegistry implementation",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a ModuleRegistry infrastructure in s-c-d that allows lookup of module coordinates by name, with support for listing, registering, and unregistering modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-08",
      "activity_name": "ModuleRegistry CLI commands",
      "activity_description": "Implement 'module info', 'module list', 'module register', and 'module unregister' commands (e.g., Spring Shell) that interact with the ModuleRegistry implementation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-09",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing and documentation",
      "activity_description": "Perform cross-module build verification, integration testing of the new features, and write minimal documentation (README updates, CLI help).",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 30
  }
}

